  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A campsite set in the hills just south of Grasse, the perfume capital, about fifteen kilometres from Cannes. A good compromise for those who want to enjoy the hinterland while staying close to the coast.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>According to several camping directories, leashed dogs are accepted in both low and high season, for a surcharge whose exact amount is not publicly stated. As usual, calling before booking lets you find out the precise terms (size, breed, rate).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the campsite is close to a golf course and a shopping centre — handy for errands, but remember to ask for a shaded pitch for the hot summer days.</div>

      <h2>With your dog: what to know</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://www.campinglapaoute.com/">campsite's official website</a> publishes no rule on animals, so sources must be cross-checked. The <a href="https://www.paysdegrassetourisme.fr/en/camping-la-paoute-919071/">Pays de Grasse tourist office</a> page (updated 2026) ticks both "pets welcome" and "<strong>pets accepted in accommodation</strong>": your dog can therefore come on a bare pitch as well as in a mobile home.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Surcharge</strong>: the motorhome portal meinwomo.net, which reuses the ACSI card data, indicates a dog surcharge of <strong>€2.50</strong> in a nightly price grid. The campsite itself does not publish this amount: have it confirmed when booking.</li>
        <li><strong>Setting</strong>: 77 pitches separated by hedges and shaded by century-old olive trees, an enclosed site closed at night according to the tourist office.</li>
        <li><strong>Opening</strong>: all year round, with a swimming pool from mid-May to end of September and a snack bar from 1 June to 15 September.</li>
        <li><strong>Not specified by the establishment</strong>: number of dogs, maximum size, possible refusal of category 1 and 2 dogs, dog left alone at the campsite, pool access, documents requested.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>With a dog, the shade of the olive trees is a real asset in summer on the Riviera. And if you're looking for an activity to share nearby, the <a href="/en/fiche-activite-club-canin-grasse">Grasse dog club</a> offers agility and training.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: put your vaccination booklet in the glove box, even if the campsite does not mention it, you may be asked for it at reception.</div>

      <h2>Worth checking before you book</h2>
      <p>The official website presents pitches separated by hedges with individual hook-ups, a sanitary block and individual bathrooms (one for people with reduced mobility), a snack bar from 1 June to 15 September, and a shopping centre nearby (100 m) and an 18-hole golf course. Dog surcharge and conditions (number, size, categories) to be confirmed by phone on 04 93 09 11 42.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Grasse's historic centre, with its perfumeries to visit, is a few minutes away by car, as are the beaches of Cannes and Mandelieu-la-Napoule.</p>
    </div>

